  // the bp domain seeds (`tacit-bp-G-v1`, `tacit-bp-H-v1`, `tacit-bp-Q-v1`)
  // or in the NUMS-H seed (`tacit-generator-H-v1`) silently shifts every
  // generator and produces proofs that no other implementation verifies.
  // Pedersen-homomorphism KAT above doesn't catch this because the seeds
  // are consistent with themselves; only the published reference vectors do.
  _kat_assertEq(H.toRawBytes(true), '02bd7bf40fb5db2f7e0a1e8660ca13df55bb0d9f904e36e6297361f00376865e56', 'NUMS H');
  // Derive only the generators we actually assert against the published
  // reference vectors. Calling _bpGens() here would force the full
  // BP_MAX_NM (=512) Gvec + 512 Hvec basis (1025 try-and-increment
  // hash-to-curve ops, ~0.5s on desktop / ~1s+ on mobile) synchronously at
  // the very front of init() — before first paint — to check 9 of those
  // points. The full basis still builds lazily on the first proof via
  // _bpGens(); these locals don't touch its memoized globals. Index 0..3 of
  // each seed are the published vectors that catch a domain-seed typo, so
  // tamper coverage of all three seeds is unchanged.
  const _Q_kat = _bpHashToCurve('tacit-bp-Q-v1', 0);
